{"parentUuid":"7578e7d0-1f96-4395-96b0-a03a4e4e5c9d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"aea371135e52bab86","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bk57612ey3EL7eG5rJ9J4z","type":"tool_result","content":"85:PLAT.MOB.notifications\tLocal & push notifications\tplatform-mobile\tE\n138:CORE.LIFE.bootstrap\tSerial bootstrap phase until the scheduler is live; hand-off to parallel init\tcore-runtime-architect\tE\t['platform-architect']\n162:CORE.TYPES.containers\tContainers (arrays, open-addressing hash maps, inline, SoA, intrusive, rings)\tcontainers-core-types\tE\n185:CORE.JOBS.test-modes\tSerial/deterministic execution mode & seeded schedule perturbation hooks\tjob-system-task-graph\tE\t['robustness-fuzzing']\n225:CORE.REFL.static-default\tStatic/compile-time reflection & resolved IDs on runtime paths; string lookup only at tool, script and serialization boundaries\treflection-metadata\tE\t['ui-architect']\n226:CORE.SER.binary\tBinary serialization\tserialization-schema\tE\n227:CORE.SER.text\tText / diff-friendly source formats\tserialization-schema\tE\t['collaboration-version-control']\n228:CORE.SER.evolution\tSchema evolution, versioning & upgraders\tserialization-schema\tE\n229:CORE.SER.relocatable\tIn-place loadable / relocatable layouts\tserialization-schema\tE\t['package-formats-vfs']\n230:CORE.SER.canonical\tDeterministic canonical serialization\tserialization-schema\tE\t['determinism-replay']\n231:CORE.SER.portability\tEndianness & ABI portability\tserialization-schema\tE\n232:CORE.SER.untrusted\tUntrusted-input validation during deserialization\tserialization-schema\tE\t['security-engineering']\n361:RND.ARCH.scene-sync\tSimulation→render extraction: change-tracked, parallel, versioned delta streams (CPU cost O(changes))\trender-architect\tE\t['geometry-pipeline', 'frame-orchestration']\n484:RND.RT.pipelines\tInline RT vs RT pipelines & shader tables\tray-tracing-infrastructure\tE\n589:PHY.CTRL.platforms\tController interaction with dynamic bodies (push, carry, ride, moving platforms)\tcharacter-physics\tE\n767:NET.SRV.persistence\tServer-authoritative persistent player/world data boundary (write-behind, leases, crash consistency, live schema migration)\tdedicated-server\tE\t['persistence-save', 'serialization-schema']\n825:GAM.SAVE.model\tSave-game model & serialization\tpersistence-save\tE\n826:GAM.SAVE.migration\tSave versioning & migration\tpersistence-save\tE\t['serialization-schema']\n877:UI.TXT.rich\tRich text, inline images, color emoji\ttext-fonts\tE\n934:ED.COLLAB.merge\tMerge tooling for scene & asset data\tcollaboration-version-control\tE\t['serialization-schema']\n1130:XC.EXT.upgrade\tEngine upgrade tooling (codemods, data upgraders)\tapi-lifecycle-migration\tE\t['serialization-schema']\n{\"_doc\": \"Every cross-cutting requirement from the brief has one owning skill that defines the obligation and reviews every other skill against it. 'obligation' is what each skill's SKILL.md must address in phase 2.\", \"concerns\": [{\"concern\": \"performance\", \"owner\": \"performance-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare budgets per tier, hot paths, and the benchmark that proves them.\"}, {\"concern\": \"memory usage\", \"owner\": \"memory-performance\", \"obligation\": \"Declare allocation strategy, memory tags, peak/steady budgets and OOM behavior (mechanisms by memory-allocators).\"}, {\"concern\": \"cache behavior\", \"owner\": \"cpu-performance\", \"obligation\": \"Declare data layouts of hot data and access patterns; justify pointer chasing.\"}, {\"concern\": \"concurrency\", \"owner\": \"concurrency-primitives\", \"obligation\": \"Declare shared state and synchronization; follow thread-safety annotation conventions.\"}, {\"concern\": \"latency\", \"owner\": \"frame-orchestration\", \"obligation\": \"Declare frame phase placement and latency contribution.\"}, {\"concern\": \"determinism\", \"owner\": \"determinism-replay\", \"obligation\": \"Declare the determinism level provided and how it is tested.\"}, {\"concern\": \"observability\", \"owner\": \"observability-telemetry\", \"obligation\": \"Declare trace zones, counters and logs; zero cost when compiled out.\"}, {\"concern\": \"debugging\", \"owner\": \"visual-debugging-tools\", \"obligation\": \"Declare debug visualizations, inspectors and console commands.\"}, {\"concern\": \"testing\", \"owner\": \"test-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Meet the test definition of done (unit, contract, integration, fuzz where untrusted).\"}, {\"concern\": \"scalability\", \"owner\": \"performance-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare behavior from the smallest to the largest configuration, scaling knobs, unit costs and asymptotic class per world-scale dimension; spatial replicas update in O(changes).\"}, {\"concern\": \"security\", \"owner\": \"security-engineering\", \"obligation\": \"Declare untrusted inputs and validation; follow the trust-boundary contract.\"}, {\"concern\": \"platform portability\", \"owner\": \"platform-architect\", \"obligation\": \"No platform code above the PAL; declare capability-tier behavior.\"}, {\"concern\": \"maintainability\", \"owner\": \"architecture-governance\", \"obligation\": \"Contracts documented, ADRs recorded, fitness functions pass.\"}, {\"concern\": \"tooling\", \"owner\": \"editor-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare authoring path, inspectors and editor integration; tool logic is domain-owned, the editor provides the host.\"}, {\"concern\": \"failure recovery\", \"owner\": \"core-runtime-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Follow the error model; declare degradation and recovery behavior.\"}, {\"concern\": \"hot reload\", \"owner\": \"hot-reload-iteration\", \"obligation\": \"Declare what reloads live and how state is preserved.\"}, {\"concern\": \"data migration\", \"owner\": \"serialization-schema\", \"obligation\": \"Version every persisted format and ship upgraders.\"}, {\"concern\": \"backwards compatibility\", \"owner\": \"api-lifecycle-migration\", \"obligation\": \"Classify APIs public/internal and follow deprecation policy.\"}, {\"concern\": \"developer usability\", \"owner\": \"developer-experience-docs\", \"obligation\": \"Ship docs, a sample, and actionable error messages.\"}, {\"concern\": \"accessibility\", \"owner\": \"accessibility\", \"obligation\": \"Map player-facing features to accessibility requirements.\"}, {\"concern\": \"evidence\", \"owner\": \"research-evidence\", \"obligation\": \"Every major decision cites graded evidence and a maturity class.\"}, {\"concern\": \"thread placement\", \"owner\": \"job-system-task-graph\", \"obligation\": \"Declare frame-phase placement, dedicated threads (via the thread inventory) and OS-thread affinity needs.\"}, {\"concern\": \"network authority & replication\", \"owner\": \"network-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare replicated state, authority, prediction/rollback participation, cosmetic-vs-simulated split and server-target behavior.\"}, {\"concern\": \"testability seams\", \"owner\": \"test-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare the test seam each external dependency uses (null device, fake backend, injectable clock, service emulator).\"}, {\"concern\": \"untrusted input\", \"owner\": \"security-engineering\", \"obligation\": \"Register every untrusted input (untrusted_inputs) with a validating owner and a fuzz target.\"}, {\"concern\": \"agent operability\", \"owner\": \"editor-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Expose debug state and controls through the agent/automation API with structured results.\"}, {\"concern\": \"external requirements\", \"owner\": \"certification-compliance\", \"obligation\": \"Satisfy the entries of the C-CERT register mapped to your capabilities.\"}, {\"concern\": \"authoring path\", \"owner\": \"editor-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Every user-facing runtime feature has tool logic in a <DOMAIN>.TOOL capability owned by the domain skill, hosted via C-EDCMD/C-EDHOST.\"}]}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"94ac73a2-19c8-4aec-9517-4d3e3d2916e1","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:22:35.179Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7578e7d0-1f96-4395-96b0-a03a4e4e5c9d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
