{"parentUuid":"7bb59a0d-619a-4bcc-94c1-e11212580868","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"aea371135e52bab86","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RUVj3b6FF8UJ2m4eC2h5VX","type":"tool_result","content":"data/milestones.json:23:    \"serialization-schema\",\ndata/milestones.json:139:    \"global-illumination\",\ndata/radar.json:193:   \"owner\": \"global-illumination\",\ndata/radar.json:204:   \"owner\": \"global-illumination\",\ndata/seed-map.json:69:  \"serialization\": [\ndata/seed-map.json:99:   \"XC.DET.levels\",\ndata/seed-map.json:159:  \"level streaming\": [\ndata/seed-map.json:215:  \"global illumination\": [\ndata/seed-map.json:228:  \"level of detail\": [\ndata/seed-map.json:625:  \"simultaneous multithreading\": [\ndata/seed-map.json:687:   \"CORE.MEM.thread-caches\"\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:39:| B2 | Task model | Work-stealing thread pool + task graph vs fiber-based jobs (Naughty Dog GDC 2015) vs C++20 coroutines | job-system-task-graph | Blocking/waiting patterns, debugger/profiler support, platform fiber support, hybrid-core scheduling behavior. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:42:| B5 | Dynamic GI | Probe volumes (DDGI class) vs surface/radiance-cache hybrid (Lumen class) vs ReSTIR GI vs baked | global-illumination | Hardware tier, dynamic-content needs, memory. Baked stays for low tiers. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:60:| B23 | Physics middleware mode | In-house vs integrated middleware with an engine-side integration layer | physics-architect | Rewind/snapshot support, determinism level, source access (see PHY.ARCH.middleware-layer). |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:61:| B24 | Server scale-out | Single-server vs zoning/instancing vs seamless meshing | network-architect, dedicated-server | Player density, world size, authority-transfer cost; meshing stays experimental. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:62:| B25 | Gameplay control model | Possession-style controller/pawn vs data-oriented control binding vs genre-specific | gameplay-architect | Genre, multiplayer model, input-to-entity cardinality. |\ndocs/08-phase-2-plan.md:34:| Constraints | performance, latency, determinism, memory, threading, platform, security, compatibility, scalability |\ndocs/08-phase-2-plan.md:46:1. **Contracts first.** Each contract owner drafts its contract specification before its SKILL.md: responsibilities, invariants, threading rules and versioning. The highest fan-in contracts come first (see `02-skill-dependency-graph.md`). Consumers review the contracts the\ndocs/08-phase-2-plan.md:63:G2 uses the same loop and stop rule as G1, applied per wave. A node converges when its assigned critics produce no accepted blocker or major findings in one round. It also needs its consumers to confirm that the contracts it provides match what they need. A wave converges \ndocs/07-research-plan.md:16:| **Core runtime, memory, concurrency** | core-runtime-architect, memory-allocators, concurrency-primitives, job-system-task-graph | ISO C++ standard papers (memory model; C++26 reflection & contracts); Intel® 64 and IA-32 Optimization Reference Manual and hybrid-archite\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:18:| **Reflection & serialization** | reflection-metadata, serialization-schema | C++26 static reflection proposals (P2996 and follow-ups); Unreal property system docs; FlatBuffers / Cap'n Proto design (schema evolution, in-place access); Frostbite and Insomniac data-pipelin\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:22:| **World & streaming** | world-architect, world-data-model, spatial-transforms | UE World Partition, One File Per Actor, Level Instances and Data Layers docs; open-world talks from Guerrilla, Ubisoft, Rockstar-adjacent public material; large-world coordinates (UE LWC doc\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:25:| **Lighting, shadows, GI, RT, PT** | direct-lighting-shadows, global-illumination, ray-tracing-infrastructure, path-tracing | ReSTIR (Bitterli et al., SIGGRAPH 2020); ReSTIR GI (Ouyang et al., HPG 2021); GRIS / ReSTIR PT (Lin et al., SIGGRAPH 2022); \"A Gentle Introductio","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"11418b22-9865-4f85-b102-9b74339d3b55","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:22:45.090Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7bb59a0d-619a-4bcc-94c1-e11212580868","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
