{"parentUuid":"1db0118b-e4fa-4593-ad65-e826dce8e88f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aea371135e52bab86","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfY3V2NMzgTsdMZ9RBFW1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found 18 findings (1 blocker, 12 major, 5 minor), written to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-2/K-LEGACY.md.\n\n`check.py` passes with 0 errors and 0 warnings. It can't see any of this because every issue is in the wording, the maturity labels or the profile tags.\n\n**Blocker**\n- **K-LEGACY-1:** capability `CORE.FRAME.pipelining` reads \"dedicated game thread and a dedicated render thread\", labelled established. That is the game-thread/render-thread split (L03) stated as owned territory. It contradicts `docs/00` §6 and `RND.GPU.recording`. `render-architect` also claims \"render threading\", and L03's justification owner (`gpu-platform-architect`) is not the skill that owns the capability (`frame-orchestration`).\n\n**Major**\n- **Tick groups under new names (2):** `CORE.FRAME.phases` (\"phase barriers\") and `CORE.FRAME.sim-schedule` (\"pre/post-physics\") recreate tick groups with barriers, which §6 claims to replace.\n- **Possession in a charter (3):** the `gameplay-architect` purpose says \"players and possession\", against L06, `GAM.FW.control` and the open ADR B25.\n- **Reflection-driven UI (4):** `UI.FW.logic` hosts UI logic through \"reflection-invoked handlers\", with no change notification in `C-UI`. That is string-based binding on the runtime path (L20).\n- **Level-bound scripting (5):** `GAM.SCR.level-scripting` and `GAM.SYS.volumes` bind logic to a whole level, which breaks under cell streaming (L18).\n- **Work-graph maturity mismatch (6):** `RND.GRAPH.work-graphs` is labelled E while the radar says X, and `RND.RHI.gpu-work` (E) bundles work graphs. This is the GPU-driven-everywhere dogma, and `check.py` does not compare radar class with capability maturity.\n- **Editor and cook code in runtime modules (7):** `CORE.ECS.baking`, `WLD.PART.cook`, `WLD.PART.hlod` and `RND.ARCH.editor-rendering` belong to runtime skills with no tool-side contracts. The tool-side proof only covers `*.TOOL.*` ids, so the editor-in-runtime pattern (L23) goes unenforced.\n- **No multiple-world support (8):** nothing requires more than one isolated world per process or forbids a global \"current world\".\n- **Replication change detection (9):** no stance on it, so per-connection property polling is the silent default.\n- **Unbatched queries (10):** `C-ENV`, `C-SPATIAL` and `C-NAV` don't require batching, which invites a virtual call per query on hot paths. `C-ENV` is the worst case, with four implementers.\n- **No shipping single-thread mode (11):** web builds without cross-origin isolation, and minimal games, have no inline mode; the only serial mode is for tests.\n- **Cell streaming everywhere (12):** the `WLD.PART.*` capabilities have no profile tags, so cell streaming ends up in card and 2D games.\n- **Catalogue gaps (13):** `legacy-patterns.json` is missing several patterns:\n  - shader compilation stutter on first use\n  - frame-rate-coupled simulation\n  - hard-reference load chains\n  - a global world\n  - replication polling\n  - a shared global random-number generator used from parallel tasks\n  - polling UI binding\n\n  No pattern links to the capabilities that carry its default stance. §6 also gives no default stance for L18–L24.\n\n**Minor**\n- **Wrong justification owners (14):** L11 and L15 name skills that don't own the code involved.\n- **Instance scene overlap (15):** `render-architect` and `geometry-pipeline` both own the GPU instance scene.\n- **Script concurrency (16):** the `C-SCRIPT` contract is silent on threading and deferred mutation.\n- **\"Main thread\" wording (17):** `RES.MGMT.no-stall` presumes a main thread.\n- **Unowned fallback (18):** the radar names a WebGL fallback that no skill owns and that isn't recorded as a non-goal.\n\nEach finding in the file includes a proposed data change. Where a check is missing, the finding says which rule to add to `check.py`: radar class equals capability maturity, a runtime/tool side for each capability, and a link from each legacy pattern to its stance capabilities.\n\nCounts: blocker 1, major 12, minor 5 — /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-2/K-LEGACY.md"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11323,"cache_read_input_tokens":143413,"output_tokens":1695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11323},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1695,"cache_read_input_tokens":143413,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11323,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfY3V24kJcFpTejKV2n7y","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ff10f2b3-3a22-4584-adf8-66f3b8299422","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:26:40.341Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
